## sendHTTPRequest (body-3)

Returns a promise whose executor creates an HTTP channel in the target document, configures request data and resolves only at fetch callback delivery.

- reads: Request fields; target window document
- writes: Configured channel and network request
- branches: Delegates branch details to nested executor.
- result: Promise resolving to {channelId}, even if callback status signals failure.
- errors: Executor throws reject, including CONNECT rejection; no status-based rejection.
- async: Adopts inner promise; request-stop callback defines completion.
- ownership: Channel lifetime is managed by network load; no cancellation exposed.

