## (anonymous) (body-4)

Creates URI/channel with loading document and cause/security defaults, annotates document HTTPS telemetry, bypasses caches anonymously, rejects CONNECT, sets method and headers with special referrer handling, optionally uploads truthy body, then starts asyncFetch.

- reads: url,method,headers,body,cause,securityFlags; document
- writes: Channel loadGroup/loadFlags/telemetry/method/headers/upload stream
- branches: Falsy security flags select default; document cause sets telemetry; CONNECT throws; optional headers/body; referer header uses referrerInfo.
- result: Starts fetch; resolve is called by nested completion callback.
- errors: URI/channel/header/upload errors throw into Promise rejection; cause.type requires cause object.
- async: Executor is synchronous until asyncFetch returns; callback later resolves.
- ownership: Body stream attached to channel; callback closes over channel and resolve.

