## getStackTrace (body-6)

Requires an active stacktrace watcher, fetches the resource stack and removes frames above debugger eval before returning.

- reads: resourceId; target watcher; stored stack
- writes: No local retained state
- branches: Missing watcher throws; sanitizer can truncate or return null for internal frames.
- result: Filtered stack array or null from sanitizer.
- errors: Throws Not listening when inactive; sanitizer/type errors propagate.
- async: Synchronous actor method; front transports result asynchronously.
- ownership: Borrows watcher stack; sanitizer slices when truncating and can return original array.

